# Shell scripts and SLURM job files run on the Linux cluster and are often copied
# there straight from a Windows working copy. With core.autocrlf=true they would
# be checked out with CRLF, and bash fails on the trailing \r with errors that
# point nowhere near the real cause. Force LF in the working copy too.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.sbatch text eol=lf
